Subject: [PATCH 09/10] fix(wire): refuse the closing overlap on the analytic
 arc path and seed the merged fixtures

Refs #3216

- seed `overlap: 0.0` in the two merged motion test literals
  (arc_lead_tests.rs, model_arcs_tests.rs): the motion lib tests compile
  again
- refuse a stated closing overlap on the drawn line-and-arc path by
  name: a tangent arc lead beside an overlap is refused at the command
  door (`overlap_refusal`), and the analytic generator
  (`wire_contour_arcs_led`) refuses any stated overlap at the
  generation door, so a stale file cannot cut a lap whose note claims a
  ride that is never made. The straight-lead polygon path
  (`ring::past_seam`) is untouched
- pin the refusals: motion lib (both leads, overlap 0 still generates)
  and the app DXF suite (create and edit doors, the reloaded file, and
  no program written)
- camcraft-mcp SKILL.md: the overlap description follows `overlap`
  again, not `lead_arc_radius`
- golden_cl.rs: fix the seeded lines' indentation
